CiviRules - PreData: skip CustomValue.get for entities that do not support custom data.

When a CiviRules trigger is registered on an entity that cannot hold custom
data (e.g. Website), CRM_Civirules_Utils_PreData::pre() still calls
civicrm_api3('CustomValue', 'get', ['entity_table' => 'Website', ...]).
Core's CRM_Core_BAO_CustomValueTable::getValues() rejects the unknown entity
type and calls CRM_Core_Error::createAPIError(), which does
`throw new Exception($msg, null)`. On PHP 8.1+ passing null to the Exception
constructor's `int $code` parameter emits an E_DEPRECATED notice
(CRM/Core/Error.php:934). The exception is caught here, so behaviour is
unchanged, but it floods the logs with one deprecation per edit of such an
entity (~8.5k lines per bulk import run, once per Organisation website write).

Guard the lookup: only entities present in
CRM_Core_SelectValues::customGroupExtends() (the same list getValues() checks)
can carry custom data. For anything else, skip the API call and leave
$customData empty — identical result, no unsupported call, no notice.

Reported against civirules 3.44.0. Remove if fixed upstream.

--- a/CRM/Civirules/Utils/PreData.php
+++ b/CRM/Civirules/Utils/PreData.php
@@ -85,11 +85,17 @@
     }
     // add custom data fields
     try {
-      $customData = civicrm_api3('CustomValue', 'get', [
-        'sequential' => 1,
-        'entity_id' => $id,
-        'entity_table' => ucfirst($entity),
-      ]);
+      $customData = [];
+      // Only entities that actually support custom data can be queried via
+      // CustomValue.get; otherwise core throws "Invalid entity type" (caught
+      // below) while emitting a PHP 8.1+ deprecation from Exception::__construct.
+      if (array_key_exists(ucfirst($entity), CRM_Core_SelectValues::customGroupExtends())) {
+        $customData = civicrm_api3('CustomValue', 'get', [
+          'sequential' => 1,
+          'entity_id' => $id,
+          'entity_table' => ucfirst($entity),
+        ]);
+      }
     }
     catch (Exception $e) {
       $customData = [];
